From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic_load_fw: print the cache address when its read fails

In system_config_8800d80(), the read-failure message of the cache-bit
block prints mem_addr (0x40500000), the address read before it, instead
of cache_mem_addr (0x40100020), the address whose read failed.

Print cache_mem_addr.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c
index a29a4e0..afa60f7 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aic_compat_8800d80.c
@@ -349,7 +349,7 @@ int system_config_8800d80(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev){
 		if (chip_mcu_id) {
 			ret = rwnx_send_dbg_mem_read_req(usb_dev, cache_mem_addr, &rd_mem_addr_cfm);
 			if (ret) {
-				printk("%x rd fail: %d\n", mem_addr, ret);
+				printk("%x rd fail: %d\n", cache_mem_addr, ret);
 				return ret;
 			}
 			rd_mem_addr_cfm.memdata |= 0x01;
